  "generated_text": "1. Determine the total number of students taking algebra:\n   - There are 24 students taking algebra.\n\n2. Determine the total number of students taking drafting:\n   - There are 11 students taking drafting only.\n   - There are 10 students taking both algebra and drafting.\n   - Therefore, the total number of students taking drafting is \\(11 + 10 = 21\\).\n\n3. Calculate the number of students taking either algebra or drafting:\n   - The number of students taking either algebra or drafting is the sum of students taking algebra and students taking drafting, minus those taking both.\n   - So, the number of students taking either algebra or drafting is \\(24 + 21 - 10 = 35\\).\n\n4. Calculate the number of students taking algebra or drafting but not both:\n   - The number of students taking algebra or drafting but not both is the number of students taking either algebra or drafting minus the number of students taking both.\n   - Therefore, the number of students taking algebra or drafting but not both is \\(35 - 10 = 25\\).\n\n\\(\\boxed{25}\\)",
